{"path":"error/error_condition","title":"std::error_condition","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>error_condition","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/error/error_condition","section":"error","kind":"page","summary":"std::error_condition holds a platform-independent value identifying an error condition.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/system_error\">&lt;system_error&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">class</span> error_condition<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><code>std::error_condition</code> holds a platform-independent value identifying an error condition. Like <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_code\">std::error_code</a></span>, it is uniquely identified by an integer value and a <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_category\">std::error_category</a></span>, but unlike <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_code\">std::error_code</a></span>, the value is not platform-dependent.\n</p><p>A typical implementation holds one integer data member (the value) and a pointer to an <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_category\">std::error_category</a></span>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Member_functions\">Member functions</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div t-dsc-member-nobold-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_condition/error_condition\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>(constructor)</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  constructs an <code>error_condition</code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_condition/operator=\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator=</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  replaces the contents <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_condition/assign\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>assign</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  replaces the contents <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_condition/clear\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>clear</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  sets the <code>error_condition</code> to value <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span> in <code>generic_category</code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_condition/value\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>value</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  obtains the value of the <code>error_condition</code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_condition/category\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>category</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  obtains the <code>error_category</code> for this <code>error_condition</code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_condition/message\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>message</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  obtains the explanatory string <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_condition/operator_bool\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator bool</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  checks if the value is non-zero <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Non-member_functions\">Non-member functions</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_condition/operator_cmp\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator==</span><span>operator!=</span><span>operator&lt;</span><span>operator&lt;=&gt;</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(removed in C++20)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(removed in C++20)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  compares <code>error_condition</code>s and <code>error_code</code>s <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Helper_classes\">Helper classes</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_condition/is_error_condition_enum\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>is_error_condition_enum</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  identifies an enumeration as an <span class=\"t-lc\"><strong class=\"selflink\">std::error_condition</strong></span> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_condition/hash\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>std::hash<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">&lt;std::error_condition&gt;</span></span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(C++17)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  hash support for <strong class=\"selflink\"><code>std::error_condition</code></strong> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template specialization)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_condition/operator_cmp\">comparison</a> between a <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_code\">std::error_code</a></span> and a <code>std::error_condition</code> is defined by their error categories. Notably, an error condition of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/generic_category\">std::generic_category</a></span> may compare equal to an error code of a specific category (e.g. <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/system_category\">std::system_category</a></span>), if they represent the same kind of error.\n</p><p>A <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/errc\">std::errc</a></span> value can be compared to an error code via implicit conversion to <code>std::error_condition</code>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cerrno&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;system_error&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;Windows.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_code\"><span class=\"kw880\">std::<span class=\"me2\">error_code</span></span></a> ec<span class=\"br0\">{</span>ERROR_FILE_EXISTS, <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/system_category\"><span class=\"kw877\">std::<span class=\"me2\">system_category</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">error_condition</span> econd<span class=\"br0\">{</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/errno_macros\"><span class=\"kw815\">EEXIST</span></a>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/generic_category\"><span class=\"kw876\">std::<span class=\"me2\">generic_category</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a>.<span class=\"me1\">setf</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">ios</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">boolalpha</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>ec <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> econd<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// typically true</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>ec <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/errc\"><span class=\"kw903\">std::<span class=\"me2\">errc</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">file_exists</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// ditto</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>ec <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> make_error_code<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/errc\"><span class=\"kw903\">std::<span class=\"me2\">errc</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">file_exists</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// false:</span>\n                                                                     <span class=\"co1\">// different category</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>true\ntrue\nfalse</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_code\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>error_code</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  holds a platform-dependent error code <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_category\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>error_category</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  base class for error categories <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/errc/make_error_condition\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>make_error_condition<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::errc)</span></span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  creates an error condition for an <code>errc</code> value <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">e</span></code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Member functions","id":"Member_functions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Non-member functions","id":"Non-member_functions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Helper classes","id":"Helper_classes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"error","title":"Diagnostics library"}],"children":[{"path":"error/error_condition/assign","title":"std::error_condition::assign"},{"path":"error/error_condition/category","title":"std::error_condition::category"},{"path":"error/error_condition/clear","title":"std::error_condition::clear"},{"path":"error/error_condition/error_condition","title":"std::error_condition::error_condition"},{"path":"error/error_condition/hash","title":"std::hash<std::error_condition>"},{"path":"error/error_condition/is_error_condition_enum","title":"std::is_error_condition_enum"},{"path":"error/error_condition/message","title":"std::error_condition::message"},{"path":"error/error_condition/operator=","title":"std::error_condition::operator="},{"path":"error/error_condition/operator_bool","title":"std::error_condition::operator bool"},{"path":"error/error_condition/operator_cmp","title":"operator==,!=,<,<=>(std::error_condition)"},{"path":"error/error_condition/value","title":"std::error_condition::value"}],"map":{"label":"std::error_condition","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++11. std::error_condition holds a platform-independent value identifying an error condition."},{"label":"Member functions","children":[{"label":"(constructor)","note":"constructs an error_condition"},{"label":"operator=","note":"replaces the contents"},{"label":"assign","note":"replaces the contents"},{"label":"clear","note":"sets the error_condition to value 0 in generic_category"},{"label":"value","note":"obtains the value of the error_condition"},{"label":"category","note":"obtains the error_category for this error_condition"},{"label":"message","note":"obtains the explanatory string"},{"label":"operator bool","n